sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Dispatcher (User)
    participant WO as Table: work_orders
    participant RES as Table: wo_items
    participant STAFF as Table: assignments
    participant LOG as Table: trips & stops
    participant FIN as Table: invoices

    Note over Admin, FIN: 1. INTAKE (The phone rings)
    Admin->>WO: INSERT new Work Order (Status: 'DRAFT')
    Admin->>RES: INSERT Item: "Generator #500" linked to WO

    Note over Admin, FIN: 2. SCHEDULING (Who is doing it?)
    Admin->>STAFF: INSERT Assignment: "John" (Role: Driver)
    Admin->>STAFF: INSERT Assignment: "Sarah" (Role: Tech)
    Admin->>WO: UPDATE Status -> 'SCHEDULED'

    Note over Admin, FIN: 3. ROUTING (How does it get there?)
    Admin->>LOG: INSERT Trip: "Truck #4" departing at 8:00 AM
    Admin->>LOG: INSERT Trip Stop: "Acme Concert Site"
    LOG->>WO: UPDATE WO to link to this Trip Stop

    Note over Admin, FIN: 4. EXECUTION (The work happens)
    Admin->>WO: UPDATE Status -> 'IN_PROGRESS' (Truck leaves)
    Admin->>WO: UPDATE Status -> 'COMPLETED' (Job done!)
    WO->>WO: UPDATE completed_at -> NOW()

    Note over Admin, FIN: 5. BILLING (Show me the money)
    Admin->>FIN: INSERT Invoice (Linked to Customer)
    Admin->>FIN: INSERT Invoice Lines (Calculated from WO Items)
    Admin->>WO: UPDATE invoice_id -> Links to new Invoice
